Making types safely reusable with
generics
In 2005, with C# 2.0 and .NET Framework 2.0, Microsoft introduced a feature named
generics, which enables your types to be more safely reusable and more efficient. It
does this by allowing a programmer to pass types as parameters, similar to how you
can pass objects as parameters.
First, let's look at an example of a non-generic type, so that you can understand the
problem that generics is designed to solve.
